      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: It's not relevant what is used, where it is, etc.  For example if i make a 5 second keyframe that animates an audio source's volume from 0 to 1, or perhaps it's pitch, it will crackle and pop the whole time... Nobody is ever able to enable audio sources directly with keyframes anywhere, gestures or otherwise, else they pop as well.  The only way anyone can activate audio cleanly is by activating a game object with said audio parented under it.  This wasn't the case months ago, but of dozens of animators i've talked to, all have run into the popping audio issue and been forced to use work-arounds just to play basic sounds even.\n\nedit:\nThe issue persists on every active frame that contains values for an audio source in it.  Even if you make it 1 frame at the start of an animation that has keyframes for other stuff, that counts as continuously animating it, even if at a constant value, therefore pops still ensue.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
