  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Whenever keyframing an audio source component, it causes it to perpetually crackle and pop.  The only way around this that has ever worked is to toggle game objects with audio source objects parented to them so keyframes never touch the audio source.\n\nThrough extensive experimentation and help of friends, we've come to determine that there is no way so solve this issue.  The only time audio can be directly keyframed without breaking is when in a world with ONSP script removed.  ONSP script in a world results in crackle.  I've also tried forcefully disabling the ONSP with keyframes on an avatar, which did effectively disable the ONSP, and restore audio to SFX instead of Avatar volume, but it did not repair the crackling problem at all.\n\nThe popping crackling broken audio is absolutely horrendous and makes animating a massive pain.\n\nThe audio needs to be fixed.",
